# Personal Portfolio — Astro + Fulldev UI

## Stack

- Framework: Astro 5 (static, no SSR unless explicitly needed)
- UI Library: fulldev/ui v0.8.x (shadcn-compatible, vanilla Astro components)
- Styling: Tailwind CSS v4 (container queries, NOT viewport breakpoints)
- TypeScript: strict mode, path alias `@/*` maps to `./src/*`
- Package manager: pnpm

## Project Layout

- `src/pages/` — Astro pages
- `src/layouts/` — Layout components (Layout.astro, etc.)
- `src/components/` — Custom components
- `src/components/ui/` — Fulldev UI components (installed via shadcn CLI, do not hand-write)
- `src/styles/` — global.css (imported from fulldev base stylesheet)
- `src/assets/` — Images and static assets

## Critical Rules

- The root layout body MUST have `class="@container"` — fulldev/ui uses container-query variants like `@2xl:` and `@max-5xl:`, NOT viewport variants like `2xl:`
- Never convert `@2xl:` / `@max-*:` Tailwind classes to plain viewport breakpoints
- Use `@/*` path aliases for all internal imports, not relative paths
- Use named exports everywhere; default exports only for Astro page files

## Never Do

- Do not hand-write components that exist in fulldev/ui — install them via the CLI
- Do not install new npm packages without asking first
- Do not use `any` in TypeScript — use `unknown` and narrow
- Do not use inline styles — use Tailwind utility classes
- Do not use React/Vue/Svelte — this is vanilla Astro only

## Git Commit Messages

When generating git commit messages:

- Follow the Conventional Commits specification.
- Use the format: <type>(<scope>): <description>
- Types: feat, fix, docs, style, refactor, test, chore.
- Keep the subject line under 60 characters.
- Use present tense (e.g., "add feature" not "added feature").
- Provide a detailed body if multiple changes are present.
